ressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, MICHIO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIDA, HIROYASU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHITOME, HIROO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU MICHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAI MITSURU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIDA HIROYASU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHITOME HIROO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMATSU, MICHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAI, MITSURU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIDA, HIROYASU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHITOME, HIROO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A fine particle comprising a porous composite oxide particle comprised of silica and an inorganic oxide other than silica and, coated thereon, a silica-based inorganic oxide layer having a thickness of 0.5 to 20 nm. The fine particle preferably contains an organic group bonded directly to a silicon atom, and the ratio of the molar amount of the silicon having the organic group bonded thereto (SR) to the molar amount of the total silicon (ST), SR/ST, is preferably 0.001 to 0.9. A substrate having a coating thereon which comprises, formed thereon, a coating film comprising the above-mentioned fine particles and a matrix for forming a film is also provided. A variety of fine particles having a structure wherein a porous composite oxide particle is coated with a porous silica-based inorganic oxide layer are provided. The formation of a coating film comprising the fine particles on a surface of a substrate results in a substrate having a coating thereon which has a low refractive index and excellent in adhesion with a resin or the like, strength, the ability to reduce reflection and the like.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur des particules fines consistant en un oxyde mixte poreux de silice et d'un oxyde minéral autre que la silice revêtu d'une couche d'oxyde minéral à base de silice d'une épaisseur de 0,5 à 20 nm. Lesdites particules contiennent de préférence un groupe organique directement lié à un atome de silicium, et le rapport Sr/St de la quantité molaire (Sr) de silicium auquel est fixé le groupe organique, à la quantité molaire du silicium total (St) est de préférence compris entre 0,001 et 0,9. L'invention porte également sur un substrat revêtu d'un film composé desdites particules et d'une matrice; elle porte en outre sur différentes particules fines consistant en un oxyde mixte poreux revêtu d'une couche d'oxyde minéral à base de silice. La formation d'un film de ces particules sur un substrat, confère à ce dernier un faible indice de réfraction, une excellente adhérence sur une résine ou analogue, une très bonne résistance, et le pouvoir de réduire les réflexions.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>